<title>USA: First Hawaiian to report Q3 charge.</title>
<headline>First Hawaiian to report Q3 charge.</headline>
<dateline>HONOLULU 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Hawaiian Inc said it will report a third quarter charge of about $0.07 a share or $2.3 million.</p>
<p>It said the charge is due to passage by the U.S. Congress of legislation to recapitalize the Savings Association Insurance Fund for thrift institutions.</p>
<p>The legislation calls for all thrift institutions nationwide to pay a one-time charge of about $0.66 per $100 of deposits to bring the insurance fund up to its designated reserve level.</p>
</text>
